---
title: "Slider"
description: "A draggable control for picking a value or a range, with keyboard support, variants, sizes, and rounded corners."
---

<script lang="ts">
	import Demo from "./demo.svelte";
</script>

# Slider

Picks a value from a range by dragging a thumb, pressing the track, or using the keyboard. Each thumb has `role="slider"`, so give the slider an `aria-label`, which passes to the thumb, or name each thumb with `thumbLabels`.

<Demo />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<script lang="ts">
	import { Slider } from "#lib/components/ui/slider/index.js";
</script>

<Slider defaultValue={[33]} max={100} step={1} aria-label="Volume" />
```

## Installation

```pm
npx remote0 add https://plainsv.com/r/slider.json
```

## Value

The value is an array with one number per thumb. Set `defaultValue` to start from a value and let the slider manage it, or use `bind:value` to read and set it from your own state. Without either, the slider starts at `min`. Values snap to `step` and stay between `min` and `max`.

## Range

Pass two values to get two thumbs with the track filled between them. Thumbs cannot pass each other, and pressing the track moves the closest one.

<Demo section="range" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<script lang="ts">
	import { Slider } from "#lib/components/ui/slider/index.js";

	let priceRange = $state([25, 75]);
</script>

<Slider bind:value={priceRange} step={5} thumbLabels={["Minimum price", "Maximum price"]} />
<p>${priceRange[0]} to ${priceRange[1]}</p>
```

## Callbacks

`onValueChange` runs on every change while dragging. `onValueCommit` runs once when a drag ends or a key moves a thumb, which suits saving or fetching.

<Demo section="commit" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<Slider defaultValue={[50]} aria-label="Volume" onValueCommit={(next) => saveVolume(next[0])} />
```

## Keyboard

Focus a thumb with Tab. The arrow keys move it by one `step`, and Shift with an arrow or Page Up and Page Down move it by ten. Home and End jump to `min` and `max`.

## Vertical

Set `orientation="vertical"` to run the track from bottom to top. A vertical slider fills its parent's height, with a minimum of `10rem`.

<Demo section="vertical" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<div style="height: 10rem">
	<Slider orientation="vertical" defaultValue={[50]} aria-label="Bass" />
</div>
```

## Forms

Set `name` to submit the slider with a form. Each value renders as a hidden input with that name, so a range submits two fields.

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<form method="POST">
	<Slider name="price" defaultValue={[25, 75]} thumbLabels={["Minimum price", "Maximum price"]} />
</form>
```

## Variants

Set `variant` to `default` or `destructive` to color the range and thumbs.

<Demo section="variants" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<Slider variant="destructive" defaultValue={[33]} aria-label="Volume" />
```

## Sizes

Set `size` to `xs`, `sm`, `md`, or `lg` to change the track thickness and thumb size. The default is `md`, and the corner radius follows the size.

<Demo section="sizes" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<Slider size="lg" defaultValue={[33]} aria-label="Volume" />
```

## Rounded

Set `rounded` to `xs` through `4xl` or `pill` to override the radius of the track and thumbs. Use `pill` for round thumbs at every size.

<Demo section="rounded" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<Slider rounded="pill" defaultValue={[33]} aria-label="Volume" />
```

## Disabled

Set `disabled` to dim the slider and block pointer and keyboard input. Disabled thumbs leave the tab order.

<Demo section="disabled" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<Slider disabled defaultValue={[33]} aria-label="Volume" />
```

## API

The `Slider` props extend the native `div` attributes, and extra attributes pass through to the root. `aria-label` and `aria-labelledby` move to each thumb instead.

```ts title="index.ts"
interface Props extends CompProps<"div"> {
	/** Thumb values from `min` to `max`, in order; supports `bind:value` */
	value?: number[];
	/** Starting values when `value` is not set; defaults to `[min]` */
	defaultValue?: number[];
	/** Lowest value; defaults to `0` */
	min?: number;
	/** Highest value; defaults to `100` */
	max?: number;
	/** Amount each value snaps to; defaults to `1` */
	step?: number;
	/** Direction of the track; `vertical` fills its parent's height */
	orientation?: "horizontal" | "vertical";
	/** Dims the slider and blocks pointer and keyboard input */
	disabled?: boolean;
	/** Form field name; each value submits as a hidden input with this name */
	name?: string;
	/** Accessible name for each thumb, such as `["Minimum", "Maximum"]`; falls back to `aria-label` */
	thumbLabels?: string[];
	/** Called with the new values on every change while dragging or typing */
	onValueChange?: (value: number[]) => void;
	/** Called with the final values when a drag ends or a key changes them */
	onValueCommit?: (value: number[]) => void;
	/** Visual style of the range and thumbs */
	variant?: "default" | "destructive";
	/** Track thickness and thumb size on the shared scale; defaults to `md` */
	size?: UiSize;
	/** Corner radius of the track and thumbs; follows `size` when omitted */
	rounded?: UiRounded;
}
```
